### The #1 Most Dangerous Web Vulnerability

SQL injection is when user input is interpreted as SQL code instead of data.

```js
// DANGEROUS: string interpolation
const query = `SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '${req.body.email}'`;

// Attacker inputs: ' OR '1'='1
// Query becomes: SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '' OR '1'='1'
// Returns ALL users!

// Attacker inputs: '; DROP TABLE users; --
// Query becomes: SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ''; DROP TABLE users; --
// Deletes the entire users table.
```

#### Prevention: Always Use Parameterized Queries

```js
// PostgreSQL (pg)
const result = await client.query(
  'SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = $1',
  [req.body.email] // Value is passed separately, never interpolated
);

// MySQL (mysql2)
const [rows] = await connection.execute(
  'SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?',
  [req.body.email]
);

// Prisma ORM (parameterized by default)
const user = await prisma.user.findUnique({
  where: { email: req.body.email }
});

// If you must write raw SQL with Prisma:
const result = await prisma.$queryRaw`
  SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ${req.body.email}
`; // Template literal tag handles escaping
```

**Rule**: Never concatenate user input into a SQL string. Always use parameterized queries or a trusted ORM.

---

### Defense in Depth with HTTP Headers

```js
import helmet from 'helmet';

// helmet sets all of these at once
app.use(helmet());

// What it sets:
// Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000     → HTTPS only
// X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN                      → No clickjacking
// X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff                  → No MIME sniffing
// Referrer-Policy: no-referrer                     → Don't leak URLs
// Permissions-Policy: geolocation=()               → Block APIs
// Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'      → Block injections
```

#### OWASP Top 10 (2021)

| # | Vulnerability | Prevention |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| A01 | Broken Access Control | Enforce RBAC, test authorization |
| A02 | Cryptographic Failures | HTTPS, bcrypt for passwords |
| A03 | Injection (SQL/XSS) | Parameterized queries, sanitize output |
| A04 | Insecure Design | Threat model during design phase |
| A05 | Security Misconfiguration | Helmet, remove defaults, patch deps |
| A06 | Vulnerable Components | `npm audit`, Dependabot |
| A07 | Auth Failures | Rate limit, MFA, strong passwords |
| A08 | Software Integrity | Sign artifacts, verify checksums |
| A09 | Logging Failures | Log all auth events and errors |
| A10 | SSRF | Validate/allowlist outbound URLs |

